{
  "//": [
    "THE SHARED IR FIXTURE SET -- read by both languages, asserted by both.",
    "",
    "`backend/tests/test_ir_validate.py` runs every case through",
    "`app.ir.validate`; `frontend/src/ir/fixtures.test.ts` runs the same",
    "cases through `frontend/src/ir/validate.ts`. Neither asserts the",
    "other's output: both assert the `code` and `loc` written down here,",
    "which were derived by hand from `docs/contracts/problem-ir.md` and",
    "from `backend/app/ir/contract.json`'s `rules` list. Two",
    "implementations that agree with each other and disagree with the",
    "contract would prove nothing.",
    "",
    "EVERY INVALID CASE IS WRONG IN EXACTLY ONE WAY. Where a structural",
    "fault makes a downstream rule unavoidably true as well (`sets` not",
    "being an array, say), the case is built on the smallest IR that",
    "isolates it -- see `mini` below -- so the named rule is the only one",
    "the document breaks.",
    "",
    "`loc` is the path INSIDE the ir. The router prefixes `body`, `ir`",
    "before it reaches a client (Ruling 30: consumers key on `loc`).",
    "",
    "Cases whose rule is `where: domain` in the contract can only be",
    "judged against real rows; the client marks them skipped and counts",
    "them, so a rule silently moving from `shape` to `domain` fails there.",
    "",
    "Three cases carry `generate` instead of `ir`: an IR big enough to",
    "break a limit is not worth 500 hand-written lines. Both harnesses",
    "build it from the spec -- `nestedAdd`, `wideAdd` and `padNote` are",
    "the only three forms, and each is about ten lines on each side.",
    "",
    "`domain` describes the world the server builds to judge the `domain`",
    "rules. It is the Workforce demo's shape (app/seed.py) minus its",
    "entities, which is what lets `workforce` below be asserted equal to",
    "the seeded IR itself."
  ],

  "domain": {
    "entityTypes": [
      {
        "name": "employee",
        "role": "agent",
        "attributes": [
          { "name": "full_name", "data_type": "text", "required": true },
          { "name": "hours_per_week", "data_type": "integer", "default_value": 40 },
          { "name": "hourly_rate", "data_type": "number", "default_value": 20.0 },
          { "name": "on_call", "data_type": "boolean", "default_value": false },
          { "name": "grade", "data_type": "enum", "enum_values": ["junior", "mid", "senior"], "default_value": "mid" },
          { "name": "hired_on", "data_type": "date" }
        ]
      },
      { "name": "unit", "role": "org", "attributes": [{ "name": "cost_centre", "data_type": "text" }] },
      {
        "name": "day",
        "role": "time",
        "attributes": [{ "name": "is_weekend", "data_type": "boolean", "default_value": false }]
      },
      {
        "name": "shift",
        "role": "time",
        "attributes": [
          { "name": "starts_at", "data_type": "time", "required": true },
          { "name": "ends_at", "data_type": "time", "required": true }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "parameters": [{ "name": "demand", "index": ["day", "shift"], "default_value": 1 }]
  },

  "valid": [
    {
      "name": "workforce",
      "why": "The seeded demo, expressed rather than merely named. A backend test asserts this is byte-for-byte what `app.seed` stores, so the seed cannot drift from the contract it is the worked example of.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["employee", "unit", "day", "shift"],
        "parameters": { "demand": { "index": ["day", "shift"] } },
        "variables": { "assign": { "index": ["employee", "day", "shift"], "domain": "binary" } },
        "constraints": [
          {
            "id": "c_cover_demand",
            "note": "each day/shift is staffed to at least demand[day, shift]",
            "forall": [{ "index": "d", "set": "day" }, { "index": "s", "set": "shift" }],
            "left": {
              "sum": { "var": "assign", "index": ["e", "d", "s"] },
              "over": [{ "index": "e", "set": "employee" }]
            },
            "relation": ">=",
            "right": { "par": "demand", "index": ["d", "s"] },
            "severity": "hard"
          },
          {
            "id": "c_one_shift_per_day",
            "note": "nobody works two shifts in a day",
            "forall": [{ "index": "e", "set": "employee" }, { "index": "d", "set": "day" }],
            "left": {
              "sum": { "var": "assign", "index": ["e", "d", "s"] },
              "over": [{ "index": "s", "set": "shift" }]
            },
            "relation": "<=",
            "right": { "const": 1 },
            "severity": "hard"
          },
          {
            "id": "c_max_hours",
            "note": "weekly hours stay within hours_per_week; every seeded shift is eight hours long",
            "forall": [{ "index": "e", "set": "employee" }],
            "left": {
              "mul": [
                { "const": 8 },
                {
                  "sum": { "var": "assign", "index": ["e", "d", "s"] },
                  "over": [{ "index": "d", "set": "day" }, { "index": "s", "set": "shift" }]
                }
              ]
            },
            "relation": "<=",
            "right": { "attr": { "of": "e", "name": "hours_per_week" } },
            "severity": "hard"
          }
        ],
        "objective": {
          "sense": "minimize",
          "terms": [
            {
              "id": "o_shifts_worked",
              "weight": 1,
              "expression": {
                "sum": { "var": "assign", "index": ["e", "d", "s"] },
                "over": [
                  { "index": "e", "set": "employee" },
                  { "index": "d", "set": "day" },
                  { "index": "s", "set": "shift" }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "mini",
      "why": "The smallest model the contract admits: one scalar binary variable, no constraints, no objective. It is the base the structural invalid cases are built on, so it has to be valid or those cases would be wrong in two ways.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": [],
        "parameters": {},
        "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } },
        "constraints": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "declared_set_need_not_be_used",
      "why": "`unit` is in `sets` and in no expression. `sets` says what the dataset must freeze, not what the arithmetic touches, so this is legal -- and it is what the seeded model does.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["day", "unit"],
        "parameters": {},
        "variables": { "open": { "index": ["day"], "domain": "binary" } },
        "constraints": []
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "soft_constraint",
      "why": "`severity: soft` with a positive integer weight -- the shape `scenario.patch`'s `soften` produces and `harden` reverses.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["day", "shift"],
        "parameters": { "demand": { "index": ["day", "shift"] } },
        "variables": { "open": { "index": ["day", "shift"], "domain": "binary" } },
        "constraints": [
          {
            "id": "c_cover",
            "forall": [{ "index": "d", "set": "day" }, { "index": "s", "set": "shift" }],
            "left": { "var": "open", "index": ["d", "s"] },
            "relation": ">=",
            "right": { "par": "demand", "index": ["d", "s"] },
            "severity": "soft",
            "weight": 100
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "filtered_sum",
      "why": "A `where` on a binding, using the expression catalogue's own `=` over a boolean attribute of the bound set: weekend days only.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["day"],
        "parameters": {},
        "variables": { "open": { "index": ["day"], "domain": "binary" } },
        "constraints": [
          {
            "id": "c_weekend_cover",
            "left": {
              "sum": { "var": "open", "index": ["d"] },
              "over": [
                { "index": "d", "set": "day", "where": [{ "attr": "is_weekend", "op": "=", "value": true }] }
              ]
            },
            "relation": ">=",
            "right": { "const": 2 },
            "severity": "hard"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "enum_filter_with_a_list_operator",
      "why": "`in` over an enum, with a list value -- the one filter operator whose value is an array. `operatorsByType` in the expression catalogue is what says an enum offers it.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["employee"],
        "parameters": {},
        "variables": { "pick": { "index": ["employee"], "domain": "binary" } },
        "constraints": [
          {
            "id": "c_seniors",
            "left": {
              "sum": { "var": "pick", "index": ["e"] },
              "over": [
                { "index": "e", "set": "employee", "where": [{ "attr": "grade", "op": "in", "value": ["mid", "senior"] }] }
              ]
            },
            "relation": ">=",
            "right": { "const": 1 },
            "severity": "hard"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "integer_variable_with_bounds",
      "why": "The other admitted variable domain. Bounds are optional and, when given, are integers -- like every other number in a v1 model.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["day"],
        "parameters": {},
        "variables": { "overtime": { "index": ["day"], "domain": "integer", "lower": 0, "upper": 4 } },
        "constraints": [
          {
            "id": "c_overtime_total",
            "left": { "sum": { "var": "overtime", "index": ["d"] }, "over": [{ "index": "d", "set": "day" }] },
            "relation": "<=",
            "right": { "const": 10 },
            "severity": "hard"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "weighted_objective_with_two_terms",
      "why": "Two terms, two ids, two weights, one sense -- and `add` used inside one of them.",
      "ir": {
        "version": 1,
        "sets": ["day"],
        "parameters": {},
        "variables": { "open": { "index": ["day"], "domain": "binary" }, "extra": { "index": [], "domain": "integer" } },
        "constraints": [],
        "objective": {
          "sense": "minimize",
          "terms": [
            {
              "id": "o_open_days",
              "weight": 1,
              "expression": { "sum": { "var": "open", "index": ["d"] }, "over": [{ "index": "d", "set": "day" }] }
            },
            {
              "id": "o_extra",
              "weight": 5,
              "expression": { "add": [{ "var": "extra", "index": [] }, { "const": 0 }] }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],

  "invalid": [
    { "code": "ir_not_object", "loc": [], "why": "an array is not a model", "ir": [] },
    { "code": "version_missing", "loc": ["version"], "why": "the document carries its version from the first one ever written", "ir": { "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "version_unsupported", "loc": ["version"], "why": "a version this platform does not express is refused, not guessed at", "ir": { "version": 2, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "key_missing", "loc": ["constraints"], "why": "a frozen model states its constraints, even when it has none", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } } } },
    { "code": "key_unknown", "loc": ["sense"], "why": "a top-level typo (here `sense` outside `objective`) is a silently ignored model half", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [], "sense": "minimize" } },

    { "code": "sets_not_array", "loc": ["sets"], "why": "snapshot_dataset() reads `sets` with jsonb_array_elements_text; an object reaches it as SQLSTATE 22023, i.e. a 500", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": { "day": 1 }, "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "set_not_a_name", "loc": ["sets", 0], "why": "entity_type.name carries the same CHECK; a name that cannot satisfy it cannot name a real type", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["Day"], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "set_duplicated", "loc": ["sets", 1], "why": "a repeated set would be frozen twice into the same key", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["day", "day"], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },

    { "code": "parameters_not_object", "loc": ["parameters"], "why": "snapshot_dataset() reads it with jsonb_object_keys", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": [], "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "parameter_not_a_name", "loc": ["parameters", "Demand"], "why": "parameter_def.name carries the same CHECK", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["day"], "parameters": { "Demand": { "index": ["day"] } }, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "parameter_not_object", "loc": ["parameters", "demand"], "why": "the declaration carries the index; an array here loses it", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["day"], "parameters": { "demand": ["day"] }, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "parameter_index_not_array", "loc": ["parameters", "demand", "index"], "why": "a parameter is indexed by an ordered, non-empty list of sets, as parameter_def.index_type_ids is", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["day"], "parameters": { "demand": { "index": "day" } }, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "parameter_index_not_declared", "loc": ["parameters", "demand", "index", 0], "why": "a parameter indexed by a set the model never declares is indexed by data the dataset will not carry", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["day"], "parameters": { "demand": { "index": ["week"] } }, "variables": { "x": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },

    { "code": "variables_not_object", "loc": ["variables"], "why": "variables are keyed by name, like parameters", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": [], "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variables_empty", "loc": ["variables"], "why": "a model with nothing to decide is not a model", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": {}, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variable_not_a_name", "loc": ["variables", "Open"], "why": "variable names are used verbatim in solution keys, so they follow the platform's one name rule", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "Open": { "index": [], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variable_not_object", "loc": ["variables", "open"], "why": "the declaration carries the index and the domain", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "open": "binary" }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variable_index_not_array", "loc": ["variables", "open", "index"], "why": "a scalar variable declares an empty index, never a missing or scalar one", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": ["day"], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "open": { "index": "day", "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variable_index_not_declared", "loc": ["variables", "open", "index", 0], "why": "a variable indexed by an undeclared set would be sized from data the dataset does not carry", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "open": { "index": ["day"], "domain": "binary" } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variable_domain_missing", "loc": ["variables", "open", "domain"], "why": "nothing may default a variable's domain: it decides the model's class", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "open": { "index": [] } }, "constraints": [] } },
    { "code": "variable_domain_unsupported", "loc": ["variables", "open", "domain"], "why": "v1 is integral by decision (spec 2: parameter values and defaults are int, for CP-SAT). A continuous variable is refused by name so the refusal says what is missing, rather than being silently absent from the vocabulary", "ir": { "version": 1, "sets": [], "parameters": {}, "variables": { "open": { "index": [], "domain": "continuous" } }, "constraints": [] } },
